{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00683",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 11.59,
      "duration_seconds": 10.63,
      "text": "Right, I'll be quick, because I've got a conference call at half ten. It's the bloating again, after I've had dairy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.88,
      "end_seconds": 20.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Then let's go straight to it. Tell me what happens after dairy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.4,
      "end_seconds": 37.26,
      "duration_seconds": 13.86,
      "text": "Within an hour, my stomach swells up like a balloon. Cheese, milk in my tea, ice cream, any of it. And then the wind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.38,
      "end_seconds": 45.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "How long does the wind and bloating last?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.06,
      "end_seconds": 51.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "A few hours. Sometimes till the next morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.28,
      "end_seconds": 63.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.02,
      "text": "Last time we talked about the irritable bowel and the tablets. How have they been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.65,
      "end_seconds": 79.09,
      "duration_seconds": 13.44,
      "text": "The mebeverine, 135 mg three times a day, maybe, I might have that wrong, it's on the packet. And the peppermint capsules, with meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.92,
      "end_seconds": 87.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "So, 135 mg, you think, and the peppermint capsules. Are they helping at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.23,
      "end_seconds": 93.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Bit. Not with dairy, though. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.15,
      "end_seconds": 102.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Any weight loss, or have you lost your appetite?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.72,
      "end_seconds": 111.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "No, no weight loss. If anything, I've put some on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.05,
      "end_seconds": 117.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Any blood in your stools, or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.68,
      "end_seconds": 122.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "No. None."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.28,
      "end_seconds": 130.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Let me remind myself of your past medical history."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.06,
      "end_seconds": 139.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Irritable bowel, iron-deficiency anaemia a few years ago, which they sorted, and migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.65,
      "end_seconds": 145.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Good. Any heartburn, or trouble swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.63,
      "end_seconds": 152.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "No, nothing like that. My swallowing's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.28,
      "end_seconds": 159.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Let me take your pulse and blood pressure. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.67,
      "end_seconds": 163.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Fine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.63,
      "end_seconds": 181.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Pulse 72, blood pressure 118 over 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.61,
      "end_seconds": 185.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Normal, then. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.32,
      "end_seconds": 193.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Normal. Tell me, what happens if you have lactose-free milk? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.18,
      "end_seconds": 204.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "Nothing. I switched my tea to lactose-free three weeks ago, and I've been fine on it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.11,
      "end_seconds": 219.08,
      "duration_seconds": 11.97,
      "text": "That's very telling. A reaction to milk and cheese, but not to lactose-free milk, makes lactose intolerance the most likely explanation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.43,
      "end_seconds": 225.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "So it's the dairy, not my IBS. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.76,
      "end_seconds": 237.36,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "Possibly both, but yes, the dairy is the likely trigger. I'd cut dairy for four weeks and see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.37,
      "end_seconds": 242.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Cheese is my weakness. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.16,
      "end_seconds": 256.03,
      "duration_seconds": 10.87,
      "text": "Hard cheeses like cheddar have very little lactose, so you may be able to keep some. Experiment. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.9,
      "end_seconds": 263.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "That's good news. And the tablets? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.61,
      "end_seconds": 278.57,
      "duration_seconds": 12.96,
      "text": "Carry on with the mebeverine and the peppermint for now, and I'll review them when we've seen what the diet does. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.4,
      "end_seconds": 285.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Right. When do I see you? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.29,
      "end_seconds": 295.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks, if that suits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.7,
      "end_seconds": 301.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Six weeks. Fine. I have to go, bye. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.77,
      "end_seconds": 306.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Take care. ~"
    }
  ]
}
